quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  4,38,And those who spend their wealth to be seen by people and do not believe in Allah or the Last Day—and whosoever has Satan as his companion has an evil companion indeed!
  4,39,What harm could have come to them if they had believed in Allah and the Last Day and spent (in charity) from the sustenance Allah had given them? And Allah is All-Knowing of them.
  4,40,"Indeed, Allah does not wrong (anyone), even by an atom’s weight. And if there is a good deed, He will double it and grant from His presence an immense reward."
  4,41,"So how shall it be, when We bring forward from every nation a witness, and (Esteemed Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) We bring you as a witness over all of them?"
  4,42,"On that Day, those who disbelieved and disobeyed the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) will wish they were swallowed up by the earth (and levelled into the dust). And they will not (be able to) conceal any statement from Allah."
  4,43,"O believers! Do not approach the prayer when you are drunk until you know (well) what you are saying, nor (enter the mosques) in a state of ritual impurity except while travelling on the road until you have washed yourselves. But if you are ill or on a journey, or any of you has come from the toilet, or you have touched women (by performing sexual intercourse), and you cannot find water, then make recourse to clean earth (for ablution), and wipe your faces and hands with it. Indeed, Allah is All-Pardoning, Most-Forgiving."
  4,44,"Have you not seen those given a share of the Scripture, purchasing misguidance and desiring that you should (also) lose the right path?"
